  "body": "From #85. Cross-hole mouths and the reach depth now use the real entry on the hole's own line, but drill_reach's cross_holder still compares the holder against the stock's corner (circumscribed) radius in the holder's Z band. Safe (never under-reads), but with mouths now at a box face the holder can be falsely refused on box stock.\n\nDone means: cross_holder reads the stock along the holder's own swept footprint (the same tube clipping cross_entry uses), keeping the corner radius only for moves that swing around the bar; pinned by a box-stock cross drill whose holder clears the face but not the corner circle and posts.",
